        ("Granada", "The city's Granada Golf Course on Granada Boulevard sets the tone: fairways and big trees with homes along the edges. A colony in a yard tree near the course is reached from your side of the property line, not across the fairway."),
        ("Country Club Prado", "The Prado is a landscaped boulevard the city has funded its own planting work on. If bees are in a tree or planter on the public part of the street rather than your lot, it is worth asking the city first."),
        ("The Biltmore area", "The Biltmore Hotel opened in 1926 and is a National Historic Landmark, with its 18-hole golf course alongside. Nearby homes and buildings share the same tile, stucco and mature trees that make bee work slower to close up neatly."),
